    <x nn="" x="70 490 867 979" f="0" si="24" te="ddd bits demultiplexer, ddd bitst are usually IRL-2 to IRL-0.\nConnects IN to one of 6 outputs.\nbit 000=R1, 001=R2, 010=RA, 011=RX, 1xx = SR or ME\nThe SR or ME output for 1xx input is selected via\nmem-read and mem-addr signals.\n\nThe setting is persistent until the next instruction fetch, when it\nwill be reset to the default. Because SR is used frequently as\nscratch register, the default should be SR, so IN refers to the\nregisters, not memory.\n\nmem-read sets SR as 1xx output regardless of the state of mem-addr,\nmem-addr without mem-read sets ME.\n\nIf the outputs are connected to the d_out signals of the 6, f.i. RA_d_out, the\ninput becomes a generic d_out (=read, for instance named SRC1).\n\nIf the outputs are connected to the d_in signals of the 6, f.i. R2_d_in, the\ninput becomes a generic d_in (=write, for instance named DST1)."/>
